{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: BR8, the browser-safe CLI module for the page. Head 3af6f41fd516e25ffba71952fe2304197044f50a, branch request/br8-browser-boundary-20261027. Main aa3ae873 is the merge base. The delta is 21 paths, 1,781 insertions and 575 deletions; the regenerated page bundle is one of them (2 lines changed). Review request 15da23b9, checker promise 56467599, request eea45d24, builder promise 561b1b81, planner ruling 14678c96. Primary artifact 6e395e42 (the PD-2 note), first of 25. gs inspect shows it resting on promise 561b1b81, request eea45d24 and ruling 14678c96.\n\nRead order: the note in full; eea45d24 and 14678c96; browser.ts, package.json, .gitattributes, the page import changes, the invitations import change and the new boundary test; the moved code (commands.ts against browser-helpers.ts, claim.ts and command-support.ts); the raw control record; the gate record; the manifest and the sealed directory. I did not run any suite again.\n\nAcceptance (eea45d24, within 14678c96):\n1. One subpath. packages/cli/package.json adds \"./browser\": \"./src/browser.ts\" beside \".\". browser.ts exports exactly ten runtime values (LINK, describe, expectedOf, heldActs, linkOf, valueOf, claim, checkClaim, issueInvitation, isInvitationIssueInput). Its other exports are types only, so Context and Outcome from commands.ts are erased and bring in no code. The page's four runtime imports, the membership-projection type import and two test mock targets now use @generalbusiness/dap-cli/browser.\n2. No Node dependencies. The new witness bundles the ten values through the actual subpath with esbuild, platform browser, and no externals or shims. It checks that:\n   - each value is identical to the main entry's export;\n   - commands.ts, line.ts, main.ts, files.ts, source.ts and both scope-index commands are not in the input graph;\n   - no input or output import is external (esbuild's own runtime helper excepted);\n   - the output exports exactly the ten names.\n   esbuild 0.28.1 was already a dependency of packages/cli; package.json, the root manifest and the lockfile are otherwise unchanged.\n3. The move preserves the code. I checked it independently of the note's AST comparison: every line removed from commands.ts, other than import lines and export keywords, appears in browser-helpers.ts, claim.ts or command-support.ts. The note's parser compared all 129 moved top-level declarations, and all 47 legacy export names remain. invitations.ts now imports its helpers from browser-helpers.ts and only types from commands.ts.\n4. The bundle is rebuilt: apps/room/page/assets.ts has a new page.js digest, and the existing asset-equality case passed. .gitattributes marks exactly the three generated bundles (the page assets, the MCP views and the brand assets) as -diff linguist-generated.\n5. The security seal follows the moved code. sourceSeal now protects commands.ts and the three new modules, and the route inventory is unchanged byte for byte.\n\nControl (raw output read). Re-exporting the same ten values through index.ts keeps the API checks passing but fails \"Runtime input closure must exclude commands.ts\" (1 failed). The restoration record shows all 18 source hashes equal before and after.\n\nValidation:\n- The ordinary gate at 049c0af9 (tree e61f8244) passed: clean, no signal, 0 contradictory records.\n- After the gate only the note and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies.\n- The manifest verifies against the sealed directory: 189 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK.\n- check-notes aa3ae873..3af6f41f reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean.\n- check-doc-links on an exported tree of the head: 713 relative links checked, 0 broken.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The page now depends on a portable module set rather than the whole CLI entry, and the command dispatcher stays Node-only. The single Stop class in command-support.ts is shared by moved and retained code, so error handling cannot split into two classes.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The moved claim, recovery, custody and invitation code is preserved line for line. No field, pin, default, route, recorded byte or authority changes. The page bundle is built from the same logic.\n\nSimplification: good. commands.ts loses about 570 lines, and the boundary is enforced by a test rather than by convention.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 3af6f41f. The builder lands. The landing closes BR8 request eea45d24. No builder deployment; the rebuilt page bundle reaches users only on the planner's next deploy.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6e395e4257aef4ba009f5bc01a38ed1cc192adc5","binding":"assigned","head":"3af6f41fd516e25ffba71952fe2304197044f50a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5646759931b32c341c29afbe2a73421e2a651db7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:561b1b81fb00c8e75277fbbce16a22112ece44a5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5646759931b32c341c29afbe2a73421e2a651db7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}